# Volkswagen Polo Mk4 (Typ 9N) five-door hatchback, 2002-2009.
#
# The 9N Polo with two round headlamps per side under clear covers (the
# four-eye front), a short bonnet and a five-door shell. The pre-facelift 9N
# is modelled; the 9N3 facelift of June 2005 with the chrome-topped grille is
# not.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volkswagen_Polo_Mk4
#
# Dimensions 3.897 x 1.650 x 1.465 m, wheelbase 2.460 m (PoloDriver,
# credited to the Volkswagen UK Press Office; Wikipedia agrees on width,
# height and wheelbase).
#
# Shape reference: no true level side elevation was available. The side image
# is a front three-quarter about 50 degrees to the side axis, the most side-on
# 9N found; the flank is reconciled against the front and rear three-quarters
# within the published dimensions. The limitation is recorded. The side and
# rear cars are the same UK five-door; the front three-quarter is a three-door.
#
# Colours: no UK brochure was retrievable, so no factory name is claimed
# (grade d). Blue, Silver, Black and Red are plain colour names; the
# photographer's note for the side car, Indigo Blue Pearl Effect, is recorded
# as a lead only. Weights 11, 10, 8, 7, total 36, provisional pending the
# central rebase.
#
# Speed 165 km/h. Comfort 70/435, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 70. Classes 1,2.
# Dates 2002-2009 production, road tail staggered 2024-2027.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vw-polo-mk4.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vw-polo-mk4.dae. References: citycars/references/vw-polo-mk4/
# (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0).
#
# Accepted deviations: no true side elevation exists, so the five-door flank was
# reconciled against the front three-quarter, rear three-quarter and detail
# images within the published dimensions; the silver three-door in the front
# three-quarter supplied only the front-end reference. Four round headlamps are
# modelled; lens internals, wheel-cover openings and rear lamp segmentation are
# simplified. The aerial, rear wiper and model lettering are omitted.


obj=citycar
name=VWPoloMk4(Blue)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=11
intro_year=2002
intro_month=2
retire_year=2027
retire_month=6
speed=165
length=3
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=70
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=435

